{
  "_": "The words that send a training question to a Translation Academy article (pipeline.ts, route `academy`). An entry is words that must all be in the question, in any order, within three words of each other (an entry starting with = only in that order, at most one word between two): `a|b` is either word, a word ending in * is a beginning (traduc* is traducir, traduzco, traducción). Words are compared without accents or capitals, and a final s does not count (idioms = idiom, modismos = modismo). The article whose longest entry matches wins; two articles tied leave the question to the other routes. `cues`: a question must have one of these words (or a \"how do I translate/say\" of commands.json) to be read as a training question at all: a word of translating, so \"Who was on the team of Paul?\" stays a Bible question. `stop`: words left out when the question's words are compared with the titles of the articles. Add words here, not rules in the code; web/tests/academy-route.test.ts checks them. Not `idioma` for idiom: in Spanish it is the language; not `perumpamaan` for simile: in Indonesian it is a parable. Another word of the question that names a Translation Words article (\"the team of horses\", \"first fruits\") cancels a match.",
